    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d795">

                <pb facs="1019" n="923" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg923"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-10-08"><hi rendition="#italic">October 8,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Your reply to our telegram as to Habana commissioners received. As we read
                    telegram of Wade to Adjutant-General it seems clear that our Cuban commissioners
                    undertook to discuss question of relinquishment of title and sovereignty and
                    advanced a proposition in relation thereto. We understood the protocol and their
                    instructions to restrict them to the military operation of evacuation, which was
                    to leave evacuated <pb facs="1020" n="924" xml:id="pg924"/> places in military
                    occupation of United States. We understand that questions as to relinquishment
                    of title and sovereignty are committed to us.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
